From 68fc0240913bee4da5a40e8152108149d7af86b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:56:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/32] perf(hc): fused hyper-connection chain behind
 SGLANG_QWENOPT_FUSE_HC=1

(A) fused_hc_mix_gate: the combine-gate logits normed . W_inject^T ride along phase 1 of the
HC mix kernel (prefetch + persistent variants; gate tiles in a separate loop on the CTAs with one
main tile fewer), so hc_combine_gate disappears.
(B) hc_fused_tail (CUDA JIT): R + y (x) 2*sigmoid(logit/hc), then the next sublayer's grouped
Gemma RMSNorm (bit-identical layout/reduction to grouped_gemma_rmsnorm), and on the MLP side
y = routed + sigmoid(h . w_sg) * shared via DeferredSharedAdd from Qwen2MoeSparseMoeBlock
(defer_shared_add, tp_size == 1 only). Per layer 9 HC launches -> 4.
qwen4_exp links each combine to the GatedResidual whose hc_norm follows it (next attn, or the
final hyper_connection_mixer; none before a PLE layer). T > 16, deterministic mode and sm100
keep the original path. Flag off: original code (additions only).
SGLANG_QWENOPT_FUSE_HC_SHARED=0 keeps the shared add in the MoE block.
